From d0936fd52562705c0badb35717c014d5998d9839 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:57:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: CPU passive
 trips and cooling maps

kaanapali.dtsi gives the CPU and CPU-LLC thermal zones only hot (120 C) and critical (125 C) trips, so the
CPUs would run unthrottled up to the critical shutdown. Stock 11.A.38 throttles from 105 C (thermal HAL,
passive) and 112/114 C (kernel). Add a 105 C passive trip (5 C hysteresis, 10 ms passive polling) to each of
the 20 CPU/CPU-LLC zones, mapped to the cpufreq cooling device of its cluster (cpu0-5 / cpu6-7). This is the
same form as the kaanapali GPU cooling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
